[[2047,124,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The supply for the centre module \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               arrives\ndirectly from the battery. (maxifuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J/B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              )\nto pin 2 via fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; the supply controlled\nby the ignition (INT) reaches pin 1 of the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pin 3 is earthed.</p><p>The standard engine temperature sender unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>K36</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               sends\na signal proportional to the temperature of the engine coolant (pin\n1) to pin 10 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              . The minimum temperature signal, on the\nother hand, arrives at pin 9 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from the engine control\nunit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>M10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>Pins 4 and 5 of the centre instrument \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>E20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               receive\nsignals (positive and negative) coming from the fuel gauge \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N40</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               located\nin the fuel pump unit.</p>"]]